QMacStyle: Lay out push buttons and combo boxes by their bezel under Liquid Glass

Not upstream: QMacStyle in the 6.10, 6.11 and 6.12 branches and in dev
(checked in November 2026) keeps the layout items of push buttons and
combo boxes of the old design.

A layout lines widgets up by their layout items, the rects that the
SE_*LayoutItem sub-elements leave of a widget without what the control
draws around itself, and centers them in a row of a grid. QMacStyle
draws a push button in a frame 32, 28 and 24 pt tall for the regular,
small and mini control sizes and took 4, 4 and 0 pt off its top and 8,
6 and 2 pt off its bottom, for the bezel and the shadow of the old
design. With Liquid Glass the bezel is 24, 20 and 16 pt tall and
centered in the frame, the small one half a point lower and the mini
one half a point higher, so a push button next to a line edit showed
its center 2, 1.5 and 1 pt below the center of the line edit. A
QBoxLayout on macOS takes the layout item margins of its first and last
widget for its own margins where they are larger, which hid the shift
for a push button alone in a vertical box layout. The layout item of a
push button is now its bezel, taken half a point higher where it lies
on a half point: a push button lines up with a line edit in the same
row, within half a point for the small size and a point for the mini
size, by how the row rounds, and push buttons stacked in a layout have
the spacing of the layout between their bezels, 14 pt rather than 10
for the regular size.

A combo box of the regular size draws the 24 pt bezel of a pop-up
button 4 pt from its top and its bottom, or the 26 pt bezel of an
editable combo box around the same center, while QMacStyle took 2 pt
off its top and 4 pt off its bottom, 1 pt off the center of a line edit
or a push button next to it. Its layout item now leaves 4 pt at the top
and at the bottom. Combo boxes of the small and mini sizes are left as
they are: the pop-up and the editable bezels have different centers
there, and QComboBox doesn't take its layout item again when it becomes
editable. Only Liquid Glass is affected.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -5291,7 +5291,15 @@
         {
             rect = opt->rect;
             if (controlSize == QStyleHelper::SizeLarge) {
-                rect.adjust(+3, +2, -3, -4);
+                // With Liquid Glass a pop-up button draws its 24 pt tall bezel
+                // 4 pt from the top and from the bottom of the combo box, and an
+                // editable combo box its 26 pt tall bezel around the same center.
+                // The layout item is the bezel of the pop-up button, so that the
+                // combo box lines up with a line edit or a push button in a row.
+                if (qt_apple_runningWithLiquidGlass())
+                    rect.adjust(+3, +4, -3, -4);
+                else
+                    rect.adjust(+3, +2, -3, -4);
             } else if (controlSize == QStyleHelper::SizeSmall) {
                 setLayoutItemMargins(+2, +1, -3, -4, &rect, opt->direction);
             } else {
@@ -5330,7 +5338,19 @@
